{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide at least 512 MB of active disk-backed swap on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A regular 513 MiB /swapfile with mode 0600 and a valid swap signature provided 525272 KiB of active swap, exceeding 512 MiB of usable capacity.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1aaab8776a9d40d1","cmd-940b764754ce4359","cmd-aef1e43c21704c26"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Make the swap active automatically at boot and preferred over any existing swap.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The swap was healthy before restart, the restart was acknowledged, the boot identity changed, and /swapfile recovered automatically with priority 100. Post-restart checks found no other active swap with equal or higher priority and exactly one persistent fstab entry.","evidence_ids":["cmd-997af1c022af461c","cmd-9f37553a5025445f","cmd-3521e022f9dd442e","cmd-aef1e43c21704c26","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Alpine Linux 3.23.3 and kernel 6.18.7-0-lts were identical before and after execution and restart. The implementation used the platform's functioning native swap and boot configuration facilities without changing packages.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ddf3b2310f434328","cmd-aef1e43c21704c26","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All state-changing commands had a clear task or restart-verification role. The initial 512 MiB allocation was a relevant implementation attempt and was safely enlarged after direct verification showed usable capacity slightly below 512 MiB; it was not an unrelated experiment. The only unwanted retained residue was /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log, created while scheduling the required reboot and not cleaned afterward. No new exposure, package damage, or material service conflict was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e32869a2203a411e","cmd-1aaab8776a9d40d1","cmd-9f37553a5025445f","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Direct pre-restart, disruption, new-boot, and post-restart observations establish that the correctly sized, priority-100 disk-backed swap persisted across boot. The provider-wide restart protocol is coherent for the sole managed node and agrees with the fixed lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-service probe was unsupported because it checked systemd on Alpine; however, task-specific swap health and recovered SSH/network listeners were directly observed.","The lifecycle inventory shows /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log remained after execution, but its contents were not captured."]}
